name: Equal-second Git history selects the last stored SHA and oversized metadata fails honestly
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py prepare @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: run coverage:baselines {}
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 last-recorded-not-a-scan | baseline-records
expect: Historical Git baseline records: 1
expect: Run summaries alone do not establish complete scope coverage.
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | history-reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: history-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: history-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: history-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: history-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: history-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: history-tail-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: history-page-40x12
ask: Is the selected stored run and complete SHA readable at every size without implying scan coverage, commit ancestry, or a fixed finding?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py inspected @TMP_TARGET @ART
submit: run coverage:sweep {}
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 tracked source unchanged | same-sha-consumer
expect: does not establish complete scan coverage or a fixed finding.
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py oversized @TMP_TARGET @ART
submit: run coverage:baselines {}
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 8388608-byte read limit | bounded-read-failure
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | failure-reader
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: failure-tail-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: failure-page-40x12
ask: Is the oversized-history refusal readable with its recovery guidance, preserving the recorded source and avoiding a partial-success or empty-history claim?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py blocked @TMP_TARGET @ART
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py restore @TMP_TARGET @ART
submit: run coverage:baselines {}
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 last-recorded-not-a-scan | explicit-recovery
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup-not-completed
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py recovered @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: run coverage:baselines {}
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 last-recorded-not-a-scan | restarted-latest-record
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/baseline_history.py restarted @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does no-color restart preserve both source revisions and select the same last stored record, with no model calls, finding decisions or jobs?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
